00:15:41.130 --> 00:15:46.230
The idea is that users save an
image to a Cloud Storage bucket

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.240
and then we have a
number of services

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:51.130
that will act on that image,
it will take that image,

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.370
it will resize that image,
it will label that image,

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.710
and it will
watermark that image,

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:59.790
and they will save them to
this output bucket, right?

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:02.520
So an image comes in, and
then it gets transformed

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.770
in multiple ways
and that image will

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.790
be saved to the output folder.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:09.990
So that's the application
image processing pipeline.

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:15.000
And the way it flows is that
first, user saves the image

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.950
to a storage bucket.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:21.520
That will trigger an event,
a new object creation event.

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:25.290
And that event will be
picked up by Eventarc Cloud

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.840
Storage trigger, so that
event will be picked up

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:31.230
and it will be passed
to a workflow, OK?

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:36.060
This workflow, it's an
image processing workflow.

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:38.700
