that event and then

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:44.320
it will call some Cloud
functions in such an order.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:46.350
So it will call a
filter function first,

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:48.180
then it will call
the labeler function,

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:50.550
and the function
will label the image

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.110
and save it to
that output bucket.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:55.115
Then it will call the resizer
bucket to resize the image

00:16:55.115 --> 00:16:56.490
and save it to
the output bucket.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.710
And it will also
call the watermarker

00:16:58.710 --> 00:17:02.070
to watermark the image and save
it to the output bucket, right?

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:05.849
And why is this
event-driven orchestration?

00:17:05.849 --> 00:17:08.910
Because we have
these functions that

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:12.660
need to be called in a certain
order with certain parameters,

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:17.040
and we put those in
orchestration with workflow.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:20.589
So this is an orchestration
that we'll go through later.

00:17:20.589 --> 00:17:22.560
But at the same time,
it's event-driven

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:27.630
because the event from Cloud
Storage through Eventarc

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.830
is starting this orchestration.

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.740
So it's loosely
coupled in that sense,

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:34.350
that an event triggers it
in a loosely coupled way,

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:37.742
but this user doesn't know
that there's an orchestration

00:17:37.742 --> 00:17:39.700
and then the orchestrator
doesn't know, really.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.390
It just gets an event
through workflows.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:46.920
So that's the event-driven
orchestration part of it.

