00:31:46.930 --> 00:31:48.970
in a little bit more
detail, because that's

00:31:48.970 --> 00:31:52.270
kind of the meat
of the code lab,

00:31:52.270 --> 00:31:54.890
how to bring these services
together with workflow.

00:31:54.890 --> 00:31:57.910
So if you look at
this workflow.yaml,

00:31:57.910 --> 00:32:00.580
you will see that
now in this workflow,

00:32:00.580 --> 00:32:03.123
we are defining how services
should be called, right?

00:32:03.123 --> 00:32:04.540
But first thing
that we need to do

00:32:04.540 --> 00:32:07.270
is that who's going to
trigger this workflow?

00:32:07.270 --> 00:32:10.400
You can either execute it
yourself, but in our case,

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:13.810
we're going to have events from
Eventarc executing it, right?

00:32:13.810 --> 00:32:16.810
So that's why we have
this first parameter

00:32:16.810 --> 00:32:20.140
event indicating
that this workflow is

00:32:20.140 --> 00:32:21.520
going to receive an event.

00:32:21.520 --> 00:32:24.400
It's actually a Cloud
event from Eventarc.

00:32:24.400 --> 00:32:25.420
Right.

00:32:25.420 --> 00:32:28.060
And then after that we
define steps, what should

00:32:28.060 --> 00:32:29.560
happen in this orchestration?

00:32:29.560 --> 00:32:32.090
The first step is
called log events,

00:32:32.090 --> 00:32:36.520
so we just log the
event that we received,

00:32:36.520 --> 00:32:39.730
just to see what we have
is useful for debugging.

00:32:39.730 --> 00:32:43.630
And then next step, we were
extracting the information

00:32:43.630 --> 00:32:44.660
that we need from event.

00:32:44.660 --> 00:32:47.718
So we are extracting the bucket
and the name from the event.

00:32:47.718 --> 00:32:49.510
So this event is going
to be a file storage

00:32:49.510 --> 00:32:52.630
event from Cloud Storage
with the bucket and the name,

00:32:52.630 --> 00:32:54.670
so we're just extracting
that and assigning them

00:32:54.670 --> 00:32:58.990
to this variables bucket
and file variable, OK?

00:32:58.990 --> 00:33:01.070
Then the next step is filter.

00:33:01.070 --> 00:33:05.380
So in this step, we are
making an HTTP post call

00:33:05.380 --> 00:33:06.850
to filter URL.

00:33:06.850 --> 00:33:09.940
Now, this filter URL, it's
a placeholder right now.

00:33:09.940 --> 00:33:12.460
We need to replace that
with the actual filter URL

00:33:12.460 --> 00:33:15.213
that we saved from
our Cloud Function.

00:33:15.213 --> 00:33:17.380
So that's why I say I have
this to do, replace here,

00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:18.838
and we'll do that
in the next step.

00:33:18.838 --> 00:33:21.610
But we will make a call
to that filter URL.

00:33:21.610 --> 00:33:23.890
And then the body
of this HTTP post,

00:33:23.890 --> 00:33:26.230
we will pass in the
bucket and the file

00:33:26.230 --> 00:33:28.240
that we receive from
the event, right?

00:33:28.240 --> 00:33:30.160
So we are basically
saying to the filter,

00:33:30.160 --> 00:33:33.850
just filter this file
in this bucket for us.

00:33:33.850 --> 00:33:36.640
The filter will have
a response, and we'll

00:33:36.640 --> 00:33:39.020
capture that response
in filter response.

00:33:39.020 --> 00:33:42.010
So that's what this is about.

00:33:42.010 --> 00:33:45.220
Now, the next step
is to log the safety,

00:33:45.220 --> 00:33:47.680
so the filter response
will have the body

00:33:47.680 --> 00:33:50.650
and the body will
have a JSON that

00:33:50.650 --> 00:33:52.280
will say safe, true or false.

00:33:52.280 --> 00:33:55.180
So we're just logging that
just so that we can see.

00:33:55.180 --> 00:33:57.550
And then after we log it, we
need to actually check it.

00:33:57.550 --> 00:34:02.020
So this check safety
actually checks the response

00:34:02.020 --> 00:34:04.870
in the body and the safe
and see if it's true.

00:34:04.870 --> 00:34:08.489
If it's true, then it will
continue with label step,

00:34:08.489 --> 00:34:10.239
so the label step is
the next step, right?

00:34:10.239 --> 00:34:11.510
It will just continue there.

00:34:11.510 --> 00:34:15.760
But if it's false, meaning
the picture is not safe,

00:34:15.760 --> 00:34:19.030
then the next step is end,
meaning this orchestration will

00:34:19.030 --> 00:34:19.721
end, right?

00:34:19.721 --> 00:34:20.679
So we check the safety.

00:34:20.679 --> 00:34:22.304
If it's not safe, we
just finish there.

00:34:22.304 --> 00:34:24.409
We don't do anything else.

00:34:24.409 --> 00:34:26.110
And then the next
step after this

00:34:26.110 --> 00:34:28.250
is that now that we
know the image is safe,

00:34:28.250 --> 00:34:33.230
we call the labeler function.

00:34:33.230 --> 00:34:36.159
Again, the labeler
URL is the placeholder

00:34:36.159 --> 00:34:38.739
that we will replace, and we
pass in the bucket and the file

00:34:38.739 --> 00:34:41.230
information, and then
we save the response

00:34:41.230 --> 00:34:45.820
of this labeler function
in the labeler response.

00:34:45.820 --> 00:34:49.137
Then we call the resizer,
again with the resizer URL

00:34:49.137 --> 00:34:50.679
and with bucket and
file, and we save

00:34:50.679 --> 00:34:52.369
the response and
the resize response,

00:34:52.369 --> 00:34:54.400
right, so very similar.

00:34:54.400 --> 00:34:58.215
And finally, we call
the watermark function.

00:34:58.215 --> 00:34:59.590
Now, with the
watermark function,

00:34:59.590 --> 00:35:00.757
we pass in more information.

00:35:00.757 --> 00:35:04.085
We pass in the bucket, the
file of the resize image.

00:35:04.085 --> 00:35:05.710
So you can see that
we are getting that

00:35:05.710 --> 00:35:07.627
from the resize response,
so we are getting it

00:35:07.627 --> 00:35:10.540
from this resize call So
that's the resize image bucket

00:35:10.540 --> 00:35:11.380
and file.

00:35:11.380 --> 00:35:14.440
And we also get the labels
from the label response,

00:35:14.440 --> 00:35:16.940
so from the label function.

00:35:16.940 --> 00:35:20.110
So the response that we get
from resize and the response

00:35:20.110 --> 00:35:23.290
that we get from label, we pass
that to our watermark function,

00:35:23.290 --> 00:35:25.030
and the watermark
will do its work

00:35:25.030 --> 00:35:28.690
and it will return a
response, as well, OK?

00:35:28.690 --> 00:35:32.490
And then finally, we have
a final step in this step.

00:35:32.490 --> 00:35:36.140
We are just returning a JSON
of filter, label, resize,

00:35:36.140 --> 00:35:39.440
and watermark, where we
just return this HTTP status

00:35:39.440 --> 00:35:44.640
code from each service, just
to see that if they work.

00:35:44.640 --> 00:35:46.640
I mean, you could return
anything else you want.

00:35:46.640 --> 00:35:48.920
You could return the URL
of the image if you like,

00:35:48.920 --> 00:35:52.640
or something else, but here I'm
just returning the HTTP code

00:35:52.640 --> 00:35:54.140
from each service.

00:35:54.140 --> 00:35:57.140
So you see how
nicely we can define

00:35:57.140 --> 00:35:59.570
what should happen in
what order and what

00:35:59.570 --> 00:36:01.400
happens with the
response and how

00:36:01.400 --> 00:36:03.980
you pass the response from
one step to another step,

00:36:03.980 --> 00:36:04.820
things like that.

00:36:04.820 --> 00:36:07.820
That's what workflow
is good for.

00:36:07.820 --> 00:36:09.650
All right, so we are in step 9.

